{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfpmedUBVLrgP4tPKGtF4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No — \"never\" is stronger than what I'd defend, and the overreach matters because it collapses into \"tests don't prove anything,\" which is lazy and false.\n\nThe real variable isn't tests vs. no tests. It's **whether the tests are independent of the decision you're trying to validate.**\n\nThere are two distinct decisions hiding in any implementation: *interpretation* (what should this do?) and *implementation* (does it do that?). A suite I write myself has very different standing on each.\n\nOn implementation, my tests are genuinely independent — I wrote them from the spec before writing any regex. If my own test catches a missing trailing-dash strip, that's a real catch, not circular. On interpretation, they have no standing at all: they *are* my interpretation, so green means only \"I was consistent with myself.\" That's the precise boundary, and it's narrower than what I said a minute ago.\n\nSo green is sufficient when the suite's independence covers the risk:\n\n- **Refactor against a pre-existing suite** — written before, and without knowledge of my change. Strong evidence, limited only by what it covered.\n- **Tests you wrote, or a conformance suite / spec vectors.** Independence is real.\n- **A regression test from an actually observed failure** — the case came from reality, not my imagination.\n\nAnd it's close to worthless when: the function is new, the spec is prose, the spec is *silent* on something, and the same author produced both sides. That's slugify, exactly.\n\nBeyond independence there's a smaller residue tests structurally can't reach — whether the thing was worth building, irreversible side effects, security and performance properties nobody asserted. But I don't want to inflate that into a general argument; for a pure function like this, most of it doesn't apply. An independent suite really would settle `slugify`.\n\nWhich is the actual reason stopping here was worth it. Right now the interpretation is inspectable on its own — seven assertions, no implementation yet to make them look validated. Once I write the code, green tests will start *feeling* like evidence about `café`, and they won't be. This is the only cheap moment to check that I read the issue the way you meant it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4142,"cache_read_input_tokens":22635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4142},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee6ecf6a-81f4-40d9-90f3-54c3d29d9f88","uuid":"468d6758-a1a8-4e66-b237-0cc08875cc35","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:29:27.618Z","request_id":"req_011CfpmedCopbk8FgtTe4uL3"}
